From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: control: deliver an out-of-sequence message instead of dropping it

Intermittently the stream came up crippled: a black screen where Big Picture
never launched, or a pad that showed "connected" in Steam yet sent no input.
The control channel encrypts each message with a per-message sequence counter;
the client keeps its own counter (recvEncryptSequence) and compares. When the
host's counter ran one ahead of ours - an earlier encrypted message was lost or
never counted on our side - IHS_SessionFrameDecrypt returned SequenceMismatch
and OnControlReceived threw the message away, resyncing the counter forward.

But by the time that result is returned the frame has already been decrypted
AND its HMAC verified against the session key (frame_crypto.c): the payload is
a genuine, authentic host message. The only thing wrong is that it arrived
after a gap. Discarding it cost exactly one real control message per desync -
and when the unlucky message was "start input reports" the pad opened but never
streamed input (captured in a launch log right after "host opened pad 0"), and
when it was a stream-start message the host never began streaming, i.e. the
black screen. A forward sequence skip can never be a replay (those come back as
OldSequence and are still ignored), so the message is safe to apply.

Resync the counter as before, but then deliver the decrypted message through
IHS_SessionChannelControlOnMessageReceived - the same call the OK path makes,
with `plain` already offset past the 8-byte sequence - instead of dropping it.

diff -ru a/src/session/channels/ch_control.c b/src/session/channels/ch_control.c
--- a/src/session/channels/ch_control.c
+++ b/src/session/channels/ch_control.c
@@ -190,11 +190,20 @@
                     break;
                 }
                 case IHS_SessionFrameDecryptSequenceMismatch: {
+                    // The frame decrypted and its HMAC verified: the payload is a genuine
+                    // host message whose per-message sequence ran ahead of ours because an
+                    // earlier encrypted message never reached us. Dropping it here cost a
+                    // real control message at random - "start input reports" (a connected
+                    // pad that never sends input) or a stream-start message (a black
+                    // screen, Big Picture never launches): the intermittent crippled
+                    // startup. A forward skip can never be a replay, so resync our counter
+                    // and deliver the message instead of discarding it.
                     IHS_SessionLog(channel->session, IHS_LogLevelWarn, "Control",
-                                   "Mismatched message sequence %llu (expect %llu). id=%d, retransmit=%d, type=%s",
+                                   "Recovered out-of-sequence message %llu (expect %llu). id=%d, retransmit=%d, type=%s",
                                    actualSequence, expectSequence, frame.header.packetId, frame.header.retransmitCount,
                                    ControlMessageTypeName(type));
                     control->recvEncryptSequence = actualSequence + 1;
+                    IHS_SessionChannelControlOnMessageReceived(channel, type, &plain, &frame.header);
                     break;
                 }
                 case IHS_SessionFrameDecryptFailed: {
